n Australia ASM list; Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information and approval records; NCBI Bookshelf/LiverTox; Epilepsy Foundation (epilepsy.com); PubMed RCT records; ClinicalTrials.gov records","reason":"Replace untrusted/inapplicable sources with trusted sources specified by audit instructions.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547871/","https://www.epilepsy.com/treatment/seizure-rescue-therapies/oral-rescue-medicines","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00319501"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=12527569-8eb3-4624-b3c0-5c0e0c5f88c9; published=Nov 15, 2024; title=LIBERVANT (DIAZEPAM) FILM [AQUESTIVE THERAPEUTICS]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=12527569-8eb3-4624-b3c0-5c0e0c5f88c9","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information; status=boxed_warning_found; Reference ID=5681158; title=VALTOCO (diazepam) nasal spray; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for black-box verification; FDA/accessdata label is permissible.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"fda_black_box_warning_verified","proposed_value":"05-20-2026","reason":"Verification should be tied to FDA/accessdata rather than DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; oral solution; rectal gel; nasal spray; IV injection; autoinjector in some settings","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; oral solution; rectal gel; nasal spray; IV/IM injection; buccal film","reason":"Add FDA-approved buccal film and remove unsupported currently available auto-injector wording.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547871/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/218623s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Diazepam 20-50 h; active metabolites up to ~100 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Diazepam half-life is formulation/population dependent: about 49.2 h after a 10 mg VALTOCO dose, about 15-100 h across adult age range after IV dosing, and desmethyldiazepam about 147 h in LIBERVANT labeling","reason":"FDA labels support a broader range and longer desmethyldiazepam half-life than the current text.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/218623s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling","reason":"Use trusted FDA/accessdata source naming instead of DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/218623s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Valium; Diastat; Diastat AcuDial; Valtoco; Libervant; diazepam rectal gel; diazepam nasal spray; diazepam buccal film; diazepam auto-injector","reason":"Alias/search field is empty despite important trade names and formulation names used in labels and RCT titles.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24111974/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"vanTuijl2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33465768/; Cereghino1998|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/; Uhari1995|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7776115/; Rosman1993|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8510706/; Autret1990|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2202804/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"vanTuijl2021|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33465768/; Cereghino1998|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/; Uhari1995|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7776115/; Rosman1993|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8510706/; Autret1990|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2202804/; Dreifuss1998|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9637805/; AbouKhalil2013|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24111974/; Alldredge2001|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","reason":"Existing links are valid but incomplete; at least three relevant placebo-controlled diazepam seizure/status epilepticus RCTs are missing.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9637805/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24111974/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11547716/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00319501","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00004297"]},{"current_value":"1.8-21 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: vanTuijl2021 diazepam for 3 days after acute stroke 1.8%; Cereghino1998 single caregiver-administered rectal diazepam dose 21%; Autret1990 intermittent oral diazepam during fever 3.5%)","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"1.8-42% (drug minus placebo seizure-free or recurrence-free differential from placebo-controlled RCTs with extractable rates: vanTuijl2021 diazepam for 3 days after acute stroke 1.8%; Dreifuss1998 diazepam rectal gel acute repetitive seizure study 42%; Cereghino1998 single caregiver-administered rectal diazepam dose 21%; Autret1990 intermittent oral diazepam during fever 3.5%)","reason":"Omitted FDA-labeled 91-patient rectal diazepam gel placebo RCT result changes the maximum differential from 21% to 42%.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9637805/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"vanTuijl2021|1.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33465768/|784; Cereghino1998|21|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/|114; Autret1990|3.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2202804/|185","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"vanTuijl2021|1.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33465768/|784; Dreifuss1998|42|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9637805/|91; Cereghino1998|21|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/|114; Autret1990|3.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2202804/|185","reason":"Add missing 42% placebo differential from the rectal diazepam gel study summarized in FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9637805/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"vanTuijl2021","pmid":"33465768","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"PMID, drug, and design verified: multicenter double-blind randomized diazepam-vs-placebo EGASIS substudy in acute stroke; abstract reports seizure occurrence 1.5% vs 3.3%. Phase label not reported.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33465768/"},{"label":"Cereghino1998","pmid":"9818845","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"PMID and study verified as randomized double-blind single-dose rectal diazepam formulation vs placebo for acute repetitive seizures; FDA labeling and trial report support 55% vs 34% seizure-free, differential 21%.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9818845/"},{"label":"Uhari1995","pmid":"7776115","proposed_action":"Retain but do not use for positive maximum-effect outcome.","rationale":"Randomized placebo-controlled febrile-seizure recurrence prevention trial of low intermittent diazepam/acetaminophen; available outcome evidence shows diazepam did not improve recurrence, so exclusion from positive seizure-freedom summary is appropriate.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7776115/"},{"label":"Rosman1993","pmid":"8510706","proposed_action":"Retain.","rationale":"PMID and design verified: randomized double-blind placebo-controlled oral diazepam during febrile illnesses; abstract reports reduced risk but does not provide simple randomized-arm seizure-free percentages for the CSV outcome plot.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8510706/"},{"label":"Autret1990","pmid":"2202804","proposed_action":"Retain with note that conclusion found no advantage.","rationale":"PMID and design verified: double-blind randomized oral diazepam-vs-placebo febrile-seizure recurrence trial; abstract reports recurrence 16% vs 19.5%, allowing recurrence-free conversion to 84% vs 80.5%, differential 3.5%.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2202804/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; Wikipedia anticonvulsant drug-class list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information and approval records; NCBI Bookshelf/LiverTox; Epilepsy Foundation (epilepsy.com); PubMed RCT records; ClinicalTrials.gov records","reason":"Current sources include non-trusted or disallowed sources for this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK547871/","https://www.epilepsy.com/treatment/seizure-rescue-therapies/oral-rescue-medicines","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00319501"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=12527569-8eb3-4624-b3c0-5c0e0c5f88c9; published=Nov 15, 2024; title=LIBERVANT (DIAZEPAM) FILM [AQUESTIVE THERAPEUTICS]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=12527569-8eb3-4624-b3c0-5c0e0c5f88c9","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata prescribing information; status=boxed_warning_found; Reference ID=5681158; title=VALTOCO (diazepam) nasal spray; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","reason":"Black-box verification must use FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA only; DailyMed is not permissible.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling","reason":"Mechanism is supported directly by FDA/accessdata labels; source text should avoid DailyMed because it is outside the trusted source list supplied for this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/211635Orig1s012corrected_lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/218623s000lbl.pdf"]}],"summary":"Diazepam row is partly verified but needs updates. Major issues: black-box warning source uses disallowed DailyMed; adverse-event percentages conflict with FDA label tables; formulations omit FDA-approved buccal film and include unsupported auto-injector availability; half-life text is too narrow; PubMed RCT list is incomplete; seizure-freedom maximum should be 42%, not 21%, once the missing rectal diazepam placebo RCT is included."}
